     1,
     "I received the following email and thought others might be interested.<div><br></div><div>karl</div><div>--------</div><div><div><br><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">Subject: </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">mqmscan vs mqmscanall</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">Date: </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">January 10, 2013 8:20:32 PM CST</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">Hi, </span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">I have been using R-QTL for a medical research project I am running and I have come across an error.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">I have successfully carried out single trait analyses using mqmscan, however when trying to perform</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">multiple trait analyses I would like to assess several traits together using mqmscanall but not</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">include sex as a phenotype in this analysis. It seems that when I get rid of the information about</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">sex and reload the file the program &quot;assumes all individuals are females&quot; and then still includes sex</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">as a phenotype in the multiple trait analysis. Is there any way to specify which phenotype columns to</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">analyse in the mqmscanall. Alternatively is there anyway to stop the read.cross function from adding</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">any information about sex? </span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">Sorry I hope this is clear. I really appreciate any help I can get, thanks very much for your time.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">Cheers</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"></div></div>"
    ]
