   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">If you have X chromosome genotypes, then sex will be needed in order to make use of it.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">But mqmscanall currently only works with *all* of the phenotypes; you can&#39;t yet specify particular columns.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">You could run the individual phenotypes of interest separately (perhaps within a for loop).</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">Or you could omit the X chromosome.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">karl</span></div>"
    ],
    [
