sex as a phenotype in this analysis. It seems that when I get rid of the information about</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">sex and reload the file the program &quot;assumes all individuals are females&quot; and then still includes sex</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">as a phenotype in the multiple trait analysis. Is there any way to specify which phenotype columns to</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">analyse in the mqmscanall. Alternatively is there anyway to stop the read.cross function from adding</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">any information about sex? </span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">Sorry I hope this is clear. I really appreciate any help I can get, thanks very much for your time.</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\">Cheers</span><br style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:monospace;font-size:medium\"></div></div></blockquote></div>"
